  "note": "X-51 art round 14: Shinkai-style sky and clouds (island.js applySkyLook; GLSL in upstream shaders/common.js skyBaseNew and world/clouds.js, switched by uFog.z). All colours linear. ?sky=old restores Petalwake's sky bit for bit. band = horizon colour on the sun side / away from it, with falloff k (bigger = thinner band); zenithPow < 1 pushes the deep blue lower; halo = Mie-like glow strengths (wide, mid, tight, core); dither = 8-bit band breaker; antiDarken = darker sky opposite the sun; sunSideWidth = how far around the horizon the warm band reaches (cos of azimuth to the sun). Clouds: sunTint x uSunColor lights the sunny edges, shade colours the shaded bases (low) and tops (top), rim = extra thin-edge gold lining (gain, power), density scales opacity, cirrus = streak layer opacity, coverage / seed drive the baked cloud map.",
